<title>JAPAN: IBJ reveals problem loans.</title>
<headline>IBJ reveals problem loans.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-05-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Industrial Bank of Japan Ltd has disclosed its restructured loans (in billions of yen unless specified):</p>
<p>					end-Mar 97     end-Mar 96</p>
<p>  Restructured loans	     92.1	    372.8</p>
<p>  Bad loans			 329.4	    121.8</p>
<p>  Non-performing loans	  402.6	    490.2</p>
<p>  Loans to troubled clients   260.2	    250.2</p>
<p>  Total problem loans	    1.08 trln	1.24 trln</p>
<p>Restructured loans are those on which interest rates have been cut to help corporate restructuring. Bad loans are to bankrupt firms and non-performing are those with interest payments in arrears by six months or more. Loans to troubled clients are mainly to the bank's non-bank affiliates.</p>
</text>
